# Downloaded spatial payloads — 1.9 GB as at 2026-08-11, same class as the two
# lines above. Re-fetchable, so the RECIPE is kept and the payload is not:
# coastal_inundation is 16 shapefile sets + their zips; flood_calibration is 47
# Copernicus EMS archives whose download URLs are recorded beside them.
# Written as `dir/*` not `dir/`, because git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded — with `dir/` every `!` below would be inert.
data/coastal_inundation/*
!data/coastal_inundation/readme.txt
data/flood_calibration/*
!data/flood_calibration/copernicus_manifest.json
!data/flood_calibration/copernicus/
data/flood_calibration/copernicus/*
!data/flood_calibration/copernicus/*.urls

# Saved HTTP error page from a failed council scrape (an "Access Denied" body,
# not a document). Kept out rather than deleted in case the failure is evidence.
/kg_dcp_page.html

# Per-session tool output, like .qa_report.json above: a hook marker and a
# cross-review result. Both are regenerated and neither describes the codebase.
.claude/.prior-art-surfaces.json
.claude/sol-shadow-review.json
# Same class, missed when the others were listed: the marker written by
# /pre-impl that gates Edit/Write to scripts/, migrations/ and services/.
# Per-session and regenerated; committing it would hand the next branch a
# stale pass for an investigation it never ran.
.claude/.pre-impl-done.json

# One rollback backup exceeds the 2 MB pre-commit gate (8.3 MB): the predicted
# December-DST shadow values behind the #883/#885 regeneration. Kept ON DISK as
# evidence — memory records that these backups must not be deleted — but out of
# git, because the gate is right that an 8 MB JSON does not belong in history.
# Every other backup in that directory is under 600 KB and IS committed.
data/db_rollback_backups/shadow_december_dst_predicted_2026-08-07.json

