# ...but NEVER the per-branch QA reports. The slug is the branch name with
# slashes as "__", so a branch called test/x or verify/x produces
# .qa/reports/test__x.json, which the three patterns above silently swallow.
# An ignored QA report is not a missing file, it is a GATE THAT STOPS
# ENFORCING: CI treats an absent report as a warning and exits 0. That is
# exactly how #398 went unnoticed for ten weeks. Found again 2026-08-12 on
# branch test/feedback-route-validation.
!.qa/reports/*.json

